  "notes": "Build-time assets that cannot live in git: upstream release binaries and multi-megabyte model files. packaging/fetch-build-assets.sh pulls each one and verifies the pinned sha256. Without this a clone of the public repository built a package that was missing them and only said so in scattered warnings. Revisions are pinned commits, never branches. The V8 voice vectors are here because data/training/** is excluded from the export: without them an OSS-built package shipped a voice missing the greeting-collapse fix, first-person-presence, refusal stability and register hold \u2014 a real behavioural difference that no warning made obvious.",
